==English==

===Etymology===
First recorded as {{m|en|shriveled|t=shrivelled}}, probably of {{bor|en|gmq|-}} origin related to dialectal {{cog|sv|skryvla|t=to wrinkle, shrivel}}; perhaps ultimately related to {{der|en|gem-pro|*skrinkwaną|t=to shrivel, shrink}} or {{m|gem-pro|*skrimpaną|t=to shrink}}.<ref>{{R:Online_Etymology_Dictionary|shrivel}}</ref>

===Pronunciation===
* {{enPR|shrĭ'vəl}}, {{IPA|en|/ˈʃɹɪvəl/}}
* {{audio|en|en-us-shrivel.ogg|a=US}}
* {{rhymes|en|ɪvəl|s=2}}

===Verb===
{{en-verb|++|pres_ptc_qual=UK|pres_ptc2=shriveling|pres_ptc2_qual=US|past_qual=UK|past2=shriveled|past2_qual=US}}

# {{lb|en|intransitive}} To [[collapse]] inward; to [[crumble]].
#: {{ux|en|The plant '''shrivelled''' from lack of water.}}
# {{lb|en|intransitive}} To become [[wrinkled]].
#: {{ux|en|His fingers were '''shriveled''' from being in the bath for too long.}}
# {{lb|en|transitive}} To draw into [[wrinkle]]s.
#: {{ux|en|The hot sun '''shrivelled''' the leaves.}}

====Derived terms====
* {{l|en|shrivel up}}

